import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns

df = sns.load_dataset("tips")
if "tip_pct" not in df.columns:
    df["tip_pct"] = (df["tip"] / df["total_bill"]) * 100

plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
sns.scatterplot(data=df, x="total_bill", y="tip_pct")
plt.title("Tip Percentage vs. Total Bill")
plt.xlabel("Total Bill")
plt.ylabel("Tip Percentage (%)")
plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()

One-Sentence Shape Description:
The plot shows a non-linear negative relationship with diminishing returns where tip_pct drops steeply at lower total_bill values and levels off as total_bill increases.


